hafner@informatik.tu-muenchen.de (Walter Hafner) writes:

>But since 3.1.1 I think Grayswandir beats them all by far! Its damage
>against the 'bread and butter' monster isn't as high as Exalibur or
>Frost Brand, but it is definitely the best weapon against all 'really
>tough' monsters - with the exceptions 'wizard' and 'angelic beings'.

Actually, according to a stats file on weapons, Grayswandir was top of
the list on both maximum and average damages for _all_ small and huge
monsters, and in second place for medium.

That's at +7, tho (maximum practical enchantment). I was surprised at the
list; Frost Brand and Grayswandir blew everything else away. Because they
both do _double_ damage, the magic bonus is doubled, too; this means that
a +7 enchantment actually adds 14 to damage. Added on to that the doubled
1-10 base (or whatever it is for sabre), and you end up with an average of
about 6 points more than, say, Excalibur. Beats Mjollnir, too; the base
damage of a war hammer is pretty pitiful.

Plus, Grayswandir is silver, so it kicks butt against silver-sensitive
beasties. Hallucination resistance is more of a nod to the amber series
than anything else, but it can be useful at low levels. 
